        <abstract>
          <p>
            <bold>syn90010</bold>
          </p>
          <p><bold>Background: </bold>Huge information from electronic oncology records can describe treatment patterns not fully represented in clinical trials. <bold>Methods: </bold>We assembled a multi-institutional dataset of 2,408 patients who progressed during CDK4/6 inhibitor therapy. Subsequent regimens and treatment durations were analyzed. <bold>Results: </bold>The most common next treatments were chemotherapy, endocrine therapy with a targeted agent, and antibody-drug conjugates. Considerable variation was observed between institutions. <bold>Conclusions: </bold>Huge information analyses may identify practice variation and inform future comparative studies. Research Sponsor: None. </p>
